176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/E (Individuals with motor impairments face significant challenges in performing daily activities due to limited or lost motor control. While Brain-Computer Interface \(BCI\) systems have shown promise in translating neural signals into actionable commands, most existing solutions are confined to laboratory settings, lacking real-time processing and practical deployment in assistive robotics. There is a need for a non-invasive, real-time BCI system that can accurately decode motor intentions from EEG signals and translate them into precise control commands for robotic arms.)
/Alt ()
/Pg 9 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
